.\" robodr-agentd(8). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-agentd/src/bin/robodr-agentd.rs and the configuration
.\" reference in crates/robodr-agentd/README.md. Keep them in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-AGENTD 8 "2026-10-26" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-agentd \- RoboDR live daemon: ROS 2 discovery and events \(-> decision chain \(-> signed black box \(-> OCSF findings spool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-agentd
.B \-\-config
.I agentd.json
.RB [ \-\-check\-config ]
.PP
.B robodr\-agentd
.RB ( \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B robodr\-agentd
reads RTPS discovery traffic (live AF_PACKET capture or a pcap replay) and
RobotEvent JSON Lines (standard input or a unix socket), runs them through
the ROS 2 pipeline and the RoboDR decision chain, records evidence in a signed
black box and writes validated OCSF findings to a spool directory. It reports
its own health and is never "OK" while blind.
.PP
It is read\-only on networks and protective only: response plans are
recorded, never executed by agentd itself; only with
.B executor.enabled
(off by default) are the reversible network actions handed to the separate
.BR robodr\-executor ,
which alone holds CAP_NET_ADMIN. It does not override the platform's safety system,
e\-stop or command authority.
.PP
Normally started by
.BR systemd (1)
as
.IR robodr\-agentd.service ,
with
.I /etc/robodr/agentd.json
and the black\-box key handed over as a systemd credential.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
The daemon configuration (JSON). Parsing is strict: unknown keys are refused at
every level, and every path must be absolute. See
.I /usr/share/doc/robodr/examples/agentd.example.json
and the crate README for the sections
.RI ( robot ", " sensor ", " policy_path ", " blackbox ", " spool ", "
.IR event_inputs ", " context ", " firewall ", " motion_monitor ", " control_plane ", " daemon ).
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate the configuration and load every file it names (profile, policy,
monitor config, key file), print warnings, then exit without starting.
The profile trust and anti\-rollback decision is made, but the state file is
not written (only a starting daemon records an accepted version).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit 0.
.SH KEY
Keys are never accepted on the command line.
.B blackbox.key_file
is either a
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1)
secret key file as written by
.B robodr\-blackbox keygen
(Ed25519 by default, or a legacy HMAC\-SHA256 key file; its key id is used,
and a
.B blackbox.key_id
that contradicts it is a configuration error) or a bare hex HMAC key of at
least 32 bytes (0.1.0\-alpha.1 format). The file is refused if it is a
symlink or not a regular file, if group or others have any access to it, if
it is owned by a uid other than the daemon's or root, if it is larger than
4 KiB, or if it is a public key file
.RI ( .pub ).
With Ed25519 the evidence is verified with the public key file alone
.RB ( "robodr\-blackbox verify \-\-keyring" " \fIFILE\fR.pub)"
and verifiers cannot forge it. HMAC keys (JSON or bare hex) are refused
unless
.B blackbox.allow_hmac
is
.BR true ;
then they load with a start\-up warning: the verifying side holds the same
secret and could forge evidence.
.PP
After an in\-place key rotation
.RB ( "robodr\-blackbox rotate" ),
.B blackbox.previous_keys
lists the retired keys' public key (or keyring) files, at most 16. They
authenticate the records signed before the rotation each time the black box
is opened, the TPM anchor sidecar written before it, and the accepted\-profile
records. A previous key must not be the current key, a key bound to a device
must name
.BR robot.id ,
an Ed25519 secret key file is refused (use its
.IR .pub ),
and an HMAC key needs
.BR blackbox.allow_hmac .
Without the key that signed a retained record the daemon refuses to start and
names
.BR blackbox.previous_keys .
.SH PROFILE TRUST
.B sensor.profile_trust
decides whether a locked profile is enforced:
.B trusted_keys
(a
.I robodr\-profile\-trust/v1
file of Ed25519 public keys; without it no locked profile is enforced),
.B state_file
(anti\-rollback: a lower
.BR profile_version ,
the same version with different bytes, or a draft replacing a locked profile
is refused),
.B allow_rollback
(the exact
.B sha256:
digest of the one older file to accept; remove it afterwards),
.B expect_platform
and
.BR expect_unit_id .
The profile must be accompanied by its detached signature
.IB profile_path .sig
as written by
.BR "robodr\-commission lock \-\-sign\-key" .
A profile that fails any check runs observe\-only and is reported as
.BR robot.ros2.profile_refused .
The profile version in findings is the signed
.BR metadata.profile_version ;
.B robot.profile_version
was removed and is refused with a message saying so.
.B trust_roots
(a
.I robodr\-trust\-roots/v1
file) enables the root\-signed
.B min_profile_version
floor and the signed revocation list
.B revocation_list
.RB ( revocation_policy :
.B optional
or
.BR required ).
With
.BR state_file ,
the newest accepted\-profile record in the black box is a second witness: a
state file that is missing or behind it raises the Critical, observe\-only
finding
.BR robot.ros2.profile_state_tampered .
.SH SAFETY STATE, CORRELATION, SIGNATURES
.B safety_feed
reads the robot's safety state passively from ROS 2 topics in the captured
traffic and/or a 0600 unix socket of JSON lines from a safety\-PLC gateway;
with a feed,
.B context.safety_state
must stay
.BR unknown .
Untrusted writers raise
.BR robot.safety_state.untrusted_source .
Nothing is ever sent to the robot or its safety system.
.PP
.B correlation
(on by default:
.BR enabled ,
.BR rules_path ,
.BR include_default_rules )
combines reported findings into
.B robot.correlate.*
findings, each recorded with every contributing finding in the black box;
observe\-only inputs make the correlation observe\-only. A rule file that
does not load is a configuration error.
.PP
.B finding_signing.key_file
names a dedicated Ed25519 key (not the black\-box key, not HMAC, same file
checks); every finding then carries a detached signature in the spooled
record's last header,
.BR robodr\-finding\-sig .
.PP
Each tick writes the black box's high\-water mark
.RI ( head.json )
when records were added; damaged closed segments quarantined at open raise
the High, observe\-only finding
.BR robot.agent.evidence_quarantined .
.SH CONTROL PLANE
.B control_plane
(off when absent) is the SOC API
.BR robodr\-control\-plane/v2
(contract
.IR /usr/share/doc/robodr/contracts/robodr.control\-plane.md ):
action requests for the seven catalog actions, judged against the live
safety state and recorded, executed only through
.B executor
(executor v1, off by default; its states are signed and journalled like
every other), and (with
.BR control_plane.evidence )
black\-box evidence exports.
.TP
.B listen_tcp\fR, \fBtls
A TCP listener. With
.B tls
.RB ( cert_chain ,
.BR key_file ,
.BR client_ca ,
optional
.BR client_spki_sha256 )
every connection is mutual TLS: the SOC's client certificate must chain to
.BR client_ca ,
be valid and, if pins are set, have a pinned public key. Without
.B tls
the address must be loopback (plain HTTP). The key file must have no
group/other permission bits.
.TP
.B unix_socket
A local socket (mode
.B socket_mode
0600 or 0660), bound with its final mode from the start.
.TP
.B state_dir
Required: a private directory (0700, owned by the daemon) holding the
request journal, the replay store and evidence exports; request states and
used nonces survive a restart.
.TP
.B soc_keys
SOC Ed25519 public key files; every request must carry a signature by one,
also over mutual TLS.
.PP
.B finding_signing
is required with
.BR control_plane :
every answer to an authenticated request, and every evidence manifest, is
signed with the finding key. Failed authentications (TLS handshakes
included) raise the High, observe\-only finding
.BR robot.agent.control_plane_unauthenticated ;
each decision, revert and export is a black\-box note.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGINT
stop the daemon cleanly: the black box is sealed and its checkpoint is copied
to the spool.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean stop (signal, or every input ended with
.BR daemon.exit_when_inputs_end ).
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure (for example the black box could not be sealed).
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error, including an argument that is not valid UTF\-8;
nothing was started. The systemd unit does not restart on this status.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/agentd.json
Configuration (operator\-created, 0640 root:robodr).
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/keys/agentd\-blackbox.key
Black\-box key (0600 root:root); the unit exposes a copy at
.IR /run/credentials/robodr\-agentd.service/blackbox.key .
.TP
.I /var/lib/robodr/blackbox/agentd/
Black\-box segments and checkpoint (single writer).
.TP
.I /var/lib/robodr/spool/agentd/
OCSF findings spool.
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/profile.json\fR, \fI/etc/robodr/profile.json.sig
Locked profile and its detached signature (0640 root:robodr).
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/profile\-trust.json
Trusted profile signing keys (public; 0644 root:root, never group/other
writable).
.TP
.I /var/lib/robodr/profile\-state/agentd.json
Anti\-rollback state (suggested path; the directory must be writable by the
daemon).
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/keys/agentd\-finding.key
Optional per\-finding signing key (0600 root:root); with the shipped drop\-in
example
.I 20\-finding\-key.conf.example
the unit exposes it at
.IR /run/credentials/robodr\-agentd.service/finding.key .
.TP
.I /var/lib/robodr/control\-plane/agentd/
Control\-plane state
.RB ( control_plane.state_dir ,
0700 robodr): request journal, replay store, evidence exports, quarantine.
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/keys/agentd\-cp\-tls.key
Optional TLS server key of the control plane (0600 root:root); with the
drop\-in example
.I 30\-control\-plane.conf.example
the unit exposes it at
.I /run/credentials/robodr\-agentd.service/cp\-tls.key
and allows the SOC network.
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/control\-plane/
The robot's certificate chain and the SOC CA bundle (public; 0644).
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/robodr/examples/robodr\-agentd.service.d/40\-sensor\-box.conf.example
Drop\-in example for a passive sensor box on a tap or port mirror
(CAP_NET_RAW only, all IP denied, waits for the
.I /var/lib/robodr
mount); install it only on a sensor box, never on a robot.
See the Unitree guide
.RI ( UNITREE.md ).
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/trust\-roots.json\fR, \fI/etc/robodr/profile\-revocations.json
Trust roots and the signed revocation list (public; 0644 root:root).
.TP
.I /run/robodr\-agentd/
Runtime directory for optional unix\-socket event and safety\-feed inputs
(socket mode 0600).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1),
.BR robodr\-replay (1),
.BR robodr\-commission (1),
.BR robodr\-diode\-pack (1),
.BR robodr\-spool\-export (1),
.BR robodr\-pulsard (8),
/usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
